      <!-- Left: Story + Explanation -->
      <div class="col-md-5">
        <p class="description">01 / Challenge</p>

        <h2>Modernizing Complex Planning Workflows Across Ontario</h2>

        <p>
          Ontario's legacy LUPIN system relied on outdated technology and manual processes, creating challenges in case coordination, data quality, and workflow visibility. OWEN aimed to modernize these services while supporting diverse user roles and Ontario's digital service standards.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>Fragmented Workflows</h3>
          <p>
            Manual processes, like email threads and disconnected communication, made cross-organizational case coordination difficult.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>Complex User Roles</h3>
          <p>
            Municipalities and partner ministries required distinct authentication, invitation, and approval workflows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3>Data Quality & Visibility</h3>
          <p>
            Inconsistent information and limited case visibility complicated planning reviews and administrative oversight.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      
