        <p class="description">
          02 / Discovery &amp; Design Approach
        </p>

        <h2>
          Rebuilding the User Experience from the Ground Up
        </h2>

        <p>
          Early usability testing revealed significant usability issues in the initial Municipality Portal, prompting a shift in design direction.

Building on existing UX research and business requirements, I rebuilt the information architecture, user flows, and UI for both external portals. Starting with Word-based smart forms, I translated evolving requirements into a new, cohesive design foundation through cross-functional collaboration.
        </p>

        <p>
          I organized feature requirements and information architecture for the two external portals, building on existing user flows before developing high-fidelity prototypes.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>


